Application secrets, e.g. the crawler's R2 credentials, are stored in Azure Key Vault: one vault per environment, `espresso-gg-{dev,prod}`.

Other states write their secrets into it, e.g. the site assets bucket's `r2-access-key-id`, and applications read them with an identity that has the "Key Vault Secrets User" role.

Read a secret with: `az keyvault secret show --vault-name espresso-gg-dev --name r2-access-key-id --query value --output tsv`
